<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper B · Learner paper</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/b/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper B</p><h1>Learner paper</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 B</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">号码: participant number</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first help at the neighbourhood event?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 前年暑假开始后的第一个周六</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年暑假结束前的最后一天</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年开学后的第一个周六</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">主角: central figure</p><p class="gloss">相册: photo album</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. Whom had the man originally regarded as the main people at the event?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 提前准备场地的人</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 等候比赛结果的邻居</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 参加比赛的人</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why does he add the other photographs and names?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为他终于找到了自己领奖的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 照片让他注意到准备工作也支持了活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为妈妈要求他删去全部比赛照片</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">思路: reasoning approach</p><p class="gloss">圈出来: circle/mark</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What help does the woman explicitly ask for?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把每道题的最终答案发给她</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 替她完成还没写的全部步骤</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 解释第二步的思路，不直接给最后答案</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What best explains the man’s final suggestion?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 认为只有把整本练习都讲完才算帮助</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 兼顾她独立思考的需要和今天有限的时间</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 准备从此不再讨论这道题</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">指示: directions/signs</p><p class="gloss">路线图: route map</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do before the design activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先替社区安装所有新的路牌</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 等活动结束后才第一次观察路口</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 画路线图，请朋友试读并记录问题</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">模型: model</p><p class="gloss">上传: upload</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What must participants prepare for Activity A?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一套自己购买的房屋模型材料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 连续三天的同一盆植物记录</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 活动结束后的三张合影</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits his interest, time and the instructions?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先做三天植物记录，再上传并等待甲的确认</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不做记录，周六直接到甲活动现场</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 报名参加周日早上的模型活动</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">草稿: draft</p><p class="gloss">封面: cover</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for choosing quotations from the book?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 苏芸</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 小杜</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 负责整理说明的女生</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What arrangement have they agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周二放学后所有人留下，一次完成整页</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 午休共同确定和检查，草稿各自在家准备</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等小杜取消训练后才开始选书</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">片段: extract/part</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What does this programme mainly offer?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 整本书逐字朗读的完整录音</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 按考试分数排列的必读书名单</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 两位读者对同一本书不同片段的推荐</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">主角: main character</p><p class="gloss">告别: say goodbye</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Acheng’s approach to feedback change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从自己写故事，变为让朋友代写全部内容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从喜欢原来的结尾，变为删去所有结尾</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从只想查错字，变为愿意听问题并补充情节</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. What attitude is best supported by the final action?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 愿意继续听意见，同时保留自己的判断</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 以后别人提出的每个改法都必须照用</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只接受指出错字、不涉及内容的意见</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">香草: herbs</p><p class="gloss">预约: reserve a place</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What must a participant do before the afternoon activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不预约，带自己的土就能直接参加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上午先整理地面才能参加下午活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先预约；需要借盒子时一起说明</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan fits the man’s circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 确认下午名额，并在预约时提出借盒子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 为了借盒子，改去自己没空的上午活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先买土和工具，再认定下午肯定能参加</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">浇水: water plants</p><p class="gloss">天气预报: weather forecast</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What is the revised meeting time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周日上午十一点</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周日早上八点</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周六早上八点</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">画具: drawing supplies</p><p class="gloss">从容: unhurried</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. How often is drawing scheduled in Xiaowen’s new weekday plan?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每个晚上连续画一个半小时</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周一和周三晚饭后各半小时</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只在每天早上出门前画十五分钟</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which combination helps explain her less rushed preparation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 完全停止画画，因此不再需要准备物品</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 坚持每天同一计划，绝不因作业量改变</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 按时收好画具，并把常用笔放在固定盒子里</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">吉他: guitar</p><p class="gloss">完美: perfect</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which suggestion fits the woman’s available time and concern?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每次都熬夜完成整幅，才算有进步</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每次练一个小部分，再留出休息时间</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先等到每天都有整晚空闲再开始</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What changed view is supported by the man’s memory of the performance?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 他开始重视共同参与的经历，而不只计算错误</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他认定以后弹琴都不需要练习</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 他证明只要有朋友在场就绝不会忘曲子</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">整理抽屉时，我发现一张旧照片，背面写着“三年前，秋天开学后的第二个周日”。那天社区第一次在小广场放电影，我和邻居一起把坐垫搬过去。电影的名字我已经记不清了，却还记得散场后大家收东西时互相道谢。照片里没有银幕，只有一排叠好的坐垫和几个笑着的人。</p></div><p class="gloss">坐垫: seat cushion</p><p class="gloss">银幕: cinema screen</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did the remembered community film event take place?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 三年前秋季开学后的第二个周日</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 三年前暑假开始后的第二个周六</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 去年秋天放假前的最后一个周日</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小时候，社区晚会结束后，我只想把自己唱歌的照片贴在墙上。我觉得那才是值得让朋友看的部分。上周整理旧相册，我发现另一张照片：我还站在台上，奶奶和几个邻居正在台边收线，两个孩子帮着把空椅子放回屋里。我当时一直等大人夸我的歌，没有注意到他们。<br>后来我问奶奶，为什么她那天没有一直坐着看。她说，中间下了一点雨，大家要把不用的东西先收好，晚会才能继续。我再看自己唱歌的照片，旁边已不是一些“不重要的人”。我请奶奶把他们的名字写下来，准备下次见面时谢谢他们。</p></div><p class="gloss">收线: gather cables</p><p class="gloss">台边: beside the stage</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. Which photographs did the writer originally want to display?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 邻居收好椅子的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 自己唱歌的照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 奶奶写下名字的照片</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why does the writer’s view of the people at the side change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 奶奶的解释把收拾物品与晚会继续联系起来</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他们后来都上台替作者唱完了歌曲</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 作者发现奶奶根本没有参加那次晚会</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小宁：周五以前请把你负责的两道例题说明发给我，我来整理成互助小组的复习页。我们约好只写解题理由，不放作业的完整答案。小博周四要训练，周五午休才能检查，所以请尽量别拖到最后。——小禾<br>小宁回复：我能按时发，但第二道题还不太明白。我不想照抄网上的说明。今晚先把自己的方法写出来，把卡住的地方标清，明天问老师，周四晚上补好。若还不能确定，我会在说明上留一句“这里待确认”，不会把猜测写成已经核对的结论。小禾，请你先整理我已经检查过的第一道题。</p></div><p class="gloss">例题: worked example</p><p class="gloss">待确认: to be confirmed</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What is Xiaoning asked to send before Friday?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 自己负责的两道例题说明</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 全班所有作业的完整答案</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小博周四训练后的照片</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. What should Xiaohe prepare for Xiaobo’s Friday check if the second method is still uncertain?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 删去待确认提示，把猜测当成正确方法发布</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求小博周四取消训练替小宁写两道题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已核对的一题，以及另一题待确认的标记</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">我对社区里的小花园很感兴趣，但还不确定以后想学什么。本月我先每周观察同一处花园，记下光照和植物变化，再向照顾花园的邻居请教。月底有一次兴趣交流，我想带着记录去听不同人的经验，而不是现在就决定未来的工作。妈妈说，先把一个问题看清楚，也是准备。</p></div><p class="gloss">光照: light conditions</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is the writer’s immediate preparation for the interest exchange?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 持续观察一处花园，记变化并请教邻居</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 立刻选定未来职业，不再比较其他兴趣</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 月底以前买下社区里的全部植物</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">兴趣体验公告：甲是周六上午的植物观察，需带连续三天的观察记录；周五中午前登记，免费。乙是周日下午的声音故事制作，不用带乐器，但须在周四前交一段自己录的生活声音；材料费十五元。两项都由社区老师带领，名额分别确认。<br>小遥给同伴的回复：我周日上午才要去看亲戚，两个活动的时间其实都能参加。不过我最想了解叶子在不同光线下的变化，已经记了两天。我没有合适的生活录音，周三和周四晚上还要排练。我准备明天再记一天，再看看甲的登记页是否还有位置。报名没确认以前，我不会把周六的名额也答应给朋友。</p></div><p class="gloss">乐器: musical instrument</p><p class="gloss">排练: rehearse</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which preparation difference is correctly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲和乙都必须自带一件乐器</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要观察记录，乙要自己录的生活声音</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲要录生活声音，乙要植物观察记录</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Why is finishing the notes and checking A’s registration a suitable next step?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为乙恰好与她周日上午探亲完全同时</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为写了两天记录就已自动取得甲的名额</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 符合她的植物兴趣，也能利用已完成的两天记录赶上登记</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">读书会公告：本周五午休交流原创短故事，每组交一页推荐材料。必须有一段不超过三句的内容简介和一条选自故事的原句，不要求每个成员都上台。周四晚八点前发来，老师会提前放到屏幕上。<br>小禾：我想做内容简介，短一点方便大家先了解故事。我放学后赶车，不能留下来练。小杜：我不太愿意站到前面，但可以找一句最能表现人物变化的话，写下为什么选它。小禾：这样我写简介，你选原句和理由。周三晚上先互相看一遍，苏芸周四午休检查，再由我晚上七点半发送。小杜：好，朗读可以请愿意的同学负责，不必为此交换我们已经答应的部分。</p></div><p class="gloss">简介: brief introduction</p><p class="gloss">原句: original sentence/quotation</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. Why does Xiaohe prefer to prepare the short introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 方便大家先了解故事，也不用放学后留下练习</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 公告规定每位成员都必须上台朗读</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她认为选取原句比介绍内容更重要</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Which division and submission plan meets both the notice and the replies?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 小杜只画封面，不选原句，周五午休再交</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每个人先上台练完，才由小禾写简介</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小禾写简介、小杜选原句，检查后周四七点半发出</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">这周读书会推荐原创故事《窗边的椅子》。故事里的女孩总把窗边的位置留给自己，后来发现新来的同学想坐那里，是为了看清黑板旁的课程表。这篇短评不替所有读者下结论，而是请大家找出女孩前后两次让座时说的话，比较她的理由。喜欢讨论人物想法的同学，可以先读这篇。</p></div><p class="gloss">让座: offer a seat</p><p class="gloss">短评: short review</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What is the main focus of the review?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公布所有读者必须接受的唯一结论</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 教授怎样画出窗边椅子的详细步骤</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 引导读者比较人物两次让座的理由</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原创故事《第三把椅子》里，阿南准备在班级小演出中讲一段最长的故事。他觉得说得越多，大家越会记得自己。排练时，小敏很少插话，只在旁边摆好三把椅子，提醒后来的人从哪里进场。阿南心想，她做的事情太少，演出时大概没人会注意。<br>正式演出前，一位同学临时忘了从哪边走，小敏用手指了指空着的椅子，他就顺利接上了。阿南讲完以后，看见观众先向小敏点头。第二天分配新任务，他没有抢着选最长的一段，而是先问小敏哪一处还需要人帮忙。他仍想讲故事，也把自己选的段落提前练好了。</p></div><p class="gloss">排练: rehearse</p><p class="gloss">进场: enter the performance area</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Which contrast best describes Anan’s changed view?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 原先想讲故事，后来拒绝准备任何段落</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 原先只重视说得多，后来也注意到安静的配合</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 原先认为演出需要合作，后来只愿自己上台</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. What can reasonably be inferred from the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 他愿意把自己的表达与小组需要一起考虑</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他已经决定有价值的工作都不能说话</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 他认为只要帮忙就不必练习自己的一段</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社区花园提案：周日上午八点集合，记录不同区域浇水前后的情况。大家两人一组，一人看老师标出的水量，一人记录。量杯和记录板由花园提供，自带水杯只供自己饮水，不能用来量浇花的水。记录时不要自己增加水量。<br>补充通知：本周入口旁的小路维修，请从西门进入，东门不开。八点到八点十五分先讲说明，第一次参加的人须听完才能开始。小安第一次来，八点前能到，想学习怎样根据记录照顾植物。他决定先找一个搭档，带好自己的饮水杯，从西门进，听完说明后再到指定区域，不因为自己来得早就先给花浇水。</p></div><p class="gloss">量杯: measuring cup</p><p class="gloss">搭档: partner</p><p class="gloss">水量: amount of water</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. Which equipment does the garden provide for recording?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每个人自己的饮水杯</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 量杯和记录板</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 用来维修入口小路的全部工具</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan satisfies both the original proposal and the update?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从东门进，用饮水杯先加水再听说明</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 八点到后独自随意加水，省去配对和说明</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从西门进，听完说明后与搭档按标示记录</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">本周社区花园试用新的记录表，只记录周末两次活动中用了多少浇花的水，不记录居民家里的用水。遇到下雨，负责人会先检查土，再决定那次是否需要浇水，并在表上说明原因。参加者不必为了让数字更小而少带自己的饮用水。试行结束后，大家一起讨论记录表哪里需要改。</p></div><p class="gloss">试行: trial implementation</p><p class="gloss">居民: residents</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. What is within the scope of this trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 检查所有居民家里的日常用水并排名</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 记录周末两次活动的浇花用水，雨天先判断是否需要</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 无论是否下雨，两次活动都必须使用同样的水量</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小圆的记录：以前我总把看喜欢的节目放在最后，常常看完才想起第二天要交的东西。最近两周，我先检查第二天的物品，再选一小段节目看。星期三有社团活动，我那天没看，也记了下来。这两周有三天早上没有再回房间找材料，出门前也多出几分钟。<br>朋友回复：你想保留看节目的兴趣，又不想临出门才找东西，可以继续试试这个顺序。要是某天事情多，少看一段或改到周末也可以。小圆补充：我愿意再记一周，尤其想看看有社团活动的那天怎样安排。现在的变化只是我这几天的感受，不能说所有人照做都会一样。</p></div><p class="gloss">顺序: sequence</p><p class="gloss">补充: add further information</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoyuan explicitly report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 两周里每天都看了完整的节目</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 有三天早上没再回房间找材料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已经不需要为第二天准备任何物品</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does the friend suggest continuing the sequence with flexible viewing?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为记录已证明人人都应按完全相同的时间表生活</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为只要不看节目，所有出门前的问题都能消失</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 它兼顾她保留兴趣和提前准备的需要，也允许忙时调整</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年学做社区节目时，我每天想把整段录音一次录好。一处读错，就从头开始，常常做到很晚。第一次播放时还是有一句不太清楚，我很失望。邻居听完却问我能不能继续介绍街边的小店，还说他记住了那家店的故事。我才发现，听众不只在数我读错的地方。<br>今年我还想做节目，但每周只有周二和周六各半小时。我准备把内容分成两小段，先核对意思，再分别录音，最后请同伴听有没有关键内容漏掉。到约好的时间就先停，不再反复从头来。周二结束后，我在本子上写的是“下次补上店主的回答”，而不是“今晚必须把所有错误都改完”。</p></div><p class="gloss">核对: check against a source</p><p class="gloss">店主: shop owner</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which current adjustment is supported by the past problem and available time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分段核对和录音，在两次半小时内完成小目标</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每次有一个读音出错就把所有录音从头重做</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不再检查关键内容，只追求录音时间更长</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What can reasonably be inferred from the note at the end?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 作者已经决定以后所有内容都交给店主完成</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 作者认为只要节目有人听，就完全不必修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 作者把下一步变得具体，并不再要求一晚消除所有错误</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to a reading-group plan</h2><p>Reply to Yao in Chinese. Say whether you can check the plan at Thursday lunchtime. Choose role-reading, a discussion of the characters or another relevant format, and explain why. State which part you can prepare. Offer a feasible adjustment to the missing speaker equipment and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安：读书小组周五要介绍我们读的短故事。你周四午休能来检查安排吗？你喜欢分角色朗读，还是讨论人物？你能先准备哪一部分？活动改在普通教室，没有音箱，原来播放背景录音的计划要改。请说说你的想法，也问清你需要知道的事。<br>小遥</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can attend the Thursday lunchtime check.</li><li>Choose a relevant format and give a reason.</li><li>State a preparation task you can take.</li><li>Address the absence of speaker equipment with a feasible adjustment.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>An unexpected problem in a shared task</h2><p>Using the fictional activity card, write connected Chinese paragraphs for a classmate about a cooperation problem and how it was handled. Include time and context, at least two actions in sequence, the contrast between your original expectation and the result, a reason or feeling, and a reflection or next step. You may add plausible details consistent with the card. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虚构经历卡<br>时间：上个月周日上午<br>任务：两人在社区花园观察，一人看、一人记录<br>原先期待：分好工，很快完成<br>意外：风吹倒水杯，记录纸湿了，部分内容看不清<br>处理：移开纸；查看同伴的现场照片；请老师一起核对；不能确认的标明，不能编数字<br>结果：比计划慢，但交出了说明问题的记录<br>感受和下一步：自行选择，与事实一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Sunday morning and a community garden observation task.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with the actual result.</li><li>Explain a feeling or reason.</li><li>Give a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Agree on a shared book recommendation</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate about a shared book recommendation. Each file already contains two plays; play it once, then allow 15 seconds to prepare and up to 30 seconds to respond. Use a reason, a past experience, a response to a new time limit and a specific next step. You may invent details. All four responses form one task /8, not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate are preparing a book recommendation for a community reading group. Personal experience may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Express a relevant need or preference.</li><li>Use a past experience to explain it.</li><li>Respond feasibly to the shorter presentation time.</li><li>Give a final arrangement, your next step and a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Recommend a community participation plan</h2><p>Recommend one of the two plans to your class. Compare a relevant feature of both, support your choice with two different details from the card, acknowledge a limitation, and propose a practical next step. Either choice can receive full credit if its constraints are handled. Prepare for 60 seconds and speak for up to 120 seconds. This task uses an on-screen card, not an audio question.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班级情况：12人，周六上午全部有空；其中8人下午也有空。希望大多数同学能参加；材料总预算50元。<br>甲：社区花园观察，周六9:00–10:00，免费，最多16人；周五12:00前提交名单；室外活动，下雨取消，不移到室内；出门前查看通知。<br>乙：邻里推荐书单，周六14:00–15:00，室内，最多12人；全组材料费40元；周五18:00前交三本书的简短介绍并报名，逾时不加人。<br>可以推荐任一方案，但须按实际时间、预算和截止要求说明参与范围与下一步。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Use one supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Use a different supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Identify a limitation of the chosen plan.</li><li>Give a next step that addresses the limitation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>